<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2647" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">an-nāvĭgo</span></b>  (better <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adn-</span></b> ), āre,
			v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to sail to</i> or <i>toward</i>, <i>to come to by ship.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>a.</b>
			<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tres (pyramides) sane conspicuae undique
					adnavigantibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 36, 12, 16</span></i>
			,  § 76.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> With <i>quo</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quo cum adnavigāsset,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					35, 10, 36, § 11</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
